  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Two elements $A$ and $B$ with atomic numbers $Z_{A}$ and $Z_{B}$ are used to produce characteristic X-rays with frequencies $v_{A}$ and $v_{B}$ respectively. If $Z_{A}: Z_{B}=1: 2,$ then $v_{A}: v_{B}$ will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "mwSan",
      "text": "$1: \\sqrt{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "HdHxp",
      "text": "$1: 8$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "vd3YS",
      "text": "$4: 1$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "AeBzb",
      "text": "$1: 4$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given $Z_{A}: Z_{B}=1: 2$ We know<br />$v \\propto Z^{2}$<br />Hence,<br />$\\begin{array}{l}<br />\\frac{v_{A}}{v_{B}}=\\frac{(1)^{2}}{(2)^{2}} \\\\<br />v_{A}: v_{B}=1: 4<br />\\end{array}$",
